.landing-how#how-it-works
  .how-container
    %h2 How a Sprint Works
    %p.how-subtitle One week. One small group. Two daily habits.
    .how-grid
      .how-step
        .how-number 1
        %h3 Join a Weekly Cohort
        %p Pick a track that fits your writing — flash fiction, poetry, personal essay — and get matched with a small group of writers like you.
      .how-step
        .how-number 2
        %h3 Write Something, Every Day
        %p Short pieces, low pressure. The goal is momentum and honesty, not a masterpiece.
      .how-step
        .how-number 3
        %h3 Critique Someone, Every Day
        %p Read a fellow writer's piece and respond with real feedback. You give a critique for every one you receive.
      .how-step
        .how-number 4
        %h3 Finish the Week Together
        %p After seven days, the cohort wraps. Go again with the same group, or start fresh with new writers next week.

.landing-features#features
  .features-container
    %h2 Built for Showing Up
    .features-grid
      .feature-card
        .feature-icon 🤝
        %h3 Matched With Real Writers
        %p Get grouped with people at your level, writing in your genre — not a faceless feed of strangers.

      .feature-card
        .feature-icon 🗓️
        %h3 Fixed-Period Commitments
        %p A week is short enough to commit to and long enough to build a habit. Sign up, show up, then decide if you go again.

      .feature-card
        .feature-icon ✍️
        %h3 Mostly Short-Form Pieces
        %p Bite-sized writing you can finish in a sitting, and critique in one too. Consistency beats length.

      .feature-card
        .feature-icon 💬
        %h3 Critiques That Go Both Ways
        %p Every writer in the cohort gives feedback and gets it back. No lurking, no one-sided asks.

      .feature-card
        .feature-icon 🔥
        %h3 Streaks That Mean Something
        %p Track your daily writing and critiquing side by side — the two habits that actually keep you improving.

      .feature-card
        .feature-icon 🌱
        %h3 A Community, Not a Void
        %p Writing is solitary by default. This makes it a little less so.

.landing-cta
  .cta-content
    %h2 Ready to Commit to a Week?
    %p Join a cohort of writers who show up daily to write and critique — and see what a week of real accountability does for your writing.
    - if account_signed_in?
      %p You're all set. Explore your dashboard and start building.
    - else
      = link_to "Create Your Free Account", new_account_session_path, class: "cta-large"
